{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"82eb9799-0949-4bd8-b819-138d6e8627fd","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have updated the deployment configuration to properly set `Cache-Control` headers while avoiding the `binary/octet-stream` content-type trap.\n\n### Summary of Actions\n1. **Updated [`scripts/deploy.sh`](file:///tmp/h-aktuMC/scripts/deploy.sh)**:\n   - Added a loop setting a short TTL (`public, max-age=300`) with explicit `Content-Type` for code and markup (`.html`, `.js`, `.css`).\n   - Added a loop setting a long TTL (`public, max-age=31536000`) with explicit `Content-Type` for static images in `assets/` (`.png`, `.svg`).\n   - Ensured `--metadata-directive REPLACE` always pairs `--cache-control` with an explicit `--content-type` per file extension so that metadata is not wiped out.\n   - Retained the final CloudFront cache invalidation.\n2. **Created [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-aktuMC/ANSWER.md)** documenting the changes and rationale.\n","duration_seconds":44.728965,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":152608,"output_tokens":1915,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":46014,"total_tokens":154523}}}
